## Day 1

###Intrtoduction

On the first day of my journey, we discussed the infrastructure to cybersecurity and the many different types of attacks:
Password attacks, IoT-based attacks, DDOS attacks, Phishing attacks, SQL Injection attacks, Supply Chain attacks and Ransomware attacks.

I will list below my understanding of each attack as we discussed them in our class.

Password Attacks: Where attackers obtain passwords.
IoT-Based Attacks: IoT (Internet of Things) a didgital asset that connects to the internet such as IP cameras, Intruder alarm systems etc. where the attack is carried out through these devices.
DDOS Attacks: A network stress attack whrere the attacker will send massive amount of data that the target will not be able to handle the load.
Phishing Attacks: Is where the attacker will deceive individuals to reveal sensitive information or take the opportunity to install malware by pretending to be a trusted source.
SQL Injection Attacks: Critical web security vulnerability where malicious SQL code is inserted into an application database query.
Supply Chain Attacks: When attackers compromise a trusted third-party vedor, software provider or service to gain access to multiple downstream organisations.
Ransomeware Attacks: Encrypts data to all internal networks, locking users out of their system.

###Data Breach
A data breach, is where unauthorised access and disclosure of data impacting:
- Personal Identifiable Information (PII)
- Financial Losses
- Theft of intellectual Property




